        "original_id": "a2306e9f-1d5f-5868-9f0c-e7afdeedd40e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Cutcliffe, Patrick Bailey\n- Organizations: Duke Blue Devils football, Ole Miss Rebels football, Walter Camp Football Foundation, Maxwell Football Club, Bobby Dodd Foundation\n- Places: Wallace Wade Stadium, Durham, North Carolina, Vaught–Hemingway Stadium, Oxford, Mississippi, Alamo Heights High School, San Antonio\n- Roles: Head coach\n\nFacts:\n- In 2002, David Cutcliffe coached the Ole Miss Rebels football team, which played its home games at Vaught–Hemingway Stadium in Oxford, Mississippi.\n- In 2004, Patrick Bailey graduated from Alamo Heights High School in San Antonio and played college football at Duke.\n- In 2013, David Cutcliffe was the Duke Blue Devils football team's head coach in his sixth year, and the team played its home games at Wallace Wade Stadium in Durham, North Carolina.\n- David Cutcliffe earned multiple college football coach of the year awards from the Walter Camp Football Foundation, the Maxwell Football Club, and the Bobby Dodd Foundation.",
